IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 19 (part roc4), DIVISION 1 -- GENERAL (rules 1 to 12), LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a definition that "means"; an "if", "only if",
--                "unless" or "except"; a flat negative; a "where", "when" or "upon" that is not met;
--                or a period the text fixes in its own words and the act is outside it.
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it lists without closing the list, "includes", is silent,
--                points to a power, a written law or a direction outside these sources, or limits a
--                grant in its own wording (a scope with no "only") and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- THE CAVEAT ON EVERY ANSWER.  O 3 r 2(1) says every requirement of the Rules is subject to the
-- Court's discretion to order otherwise; no function here threads it as an input (PLAN.md section 2).
--
-- WHAT THIS ORDER DEFINES FOR ITSELF.  Rule 3 defines "judgment", "trial", "record of appeal" and the
-- rest for this Order; rule 13(2) defines "lower Court" for Division 2.  Where this Order redefines
-- a word the core or O 1 r 3(1) also uses, this module declares its own type under its own label and
-- does not call the keel's function.  Inside this file "the appellate Court" and "the lower Court" are
-- not given a keel type: each rule says which court it means in its own name.
--
-- TIME.  The count of a period is O 3 r 3 (roc1's range) and an extension is O 3 r 4 (roc1's range).
-- Every timed rule below takes the last day as an INPUT, `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`, and
-- the last day as extended or shortened, `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`
-- (NOTHING = no extension or shortening).  The date a document is filed or served is the date it counts
-- as filed (O 28 r 10) or as served (O 7 r 8, O 28 r 12), which the caller supplies.
-- Each period is a core `Period` constant named for its section, so the number appears once.
-- Outside a period the text fixes in its own words the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The one helper every timed rule in this Order calls.  It answers a structural question
-- (is a date on or before the last day that counts) and no legal one.  It takes the label of the
-- first timed rule that needs it, O 19 r 8(3).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVEN `the date the act is done` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`
    WHEN JUST extended THEN `the date the act is done` AT MOST extended
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the act is done` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

-- The same for an act of two parts (file, then serve): both dates must be on or before the last day.
GIVEN `the date the document is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the document is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` MEANS
        `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` `the date the document is filed` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`
    AND `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` `the date the document is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 19 -- Division 1 -- General`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- scope of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What was decided, in the lower Court's judgment: the kinds of case that rule 3 lists as a "judgment".
DECLARE `o 19 r 3 kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`
    `o 19 r 3(a) a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent`
    `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`
    `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court`
    `o 19 r 3(d) an application for a prerogative order`
    `o 19 r 3(e) an appeal against a judgment described in paragraphs (a) to (d)`
    `o 19 r 3 any other decision`

-- The judgment an appeal is brought against, as a witness would describe it.
DECLARE `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` HAS
    `o 19 r 1 court that gave it`         IS A `Court level`
    `o 19 r 1 who gave it`                IS A `Decision maker`
    `o 19 r 1 what it was given in`       IS A `o 19 r 3 kind of decision`
    `o 19 r 1 the proceedings began with` IS A `Document kind`
    `o 19 r 1 damages or accounts by a District Judge` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The matters rule 1 sorts: the six kinds in paragraphs (a) to (f), and anything else.
DECLARE `o 19 r 1 matter` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` HAS `o 19 r 1 the judgment` IS A `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against`
    `o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` HAS
        `o 19 r 1(d) to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
        `o 19 r 1(d) pursuant to a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 1 an application to the appellate Court` HAS
        `o 19 r 1(e) relating to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 1 an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`
    `o 19 r 1 any other matter`

-- src:2235 | 1. This Order applies to — ( a )
-- src:2236 | an appeal against any judgment of a Magistrate’s Court or District Court given — (i)
-- src:2237 | in a trial of an originating claim, including a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent; [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:2238 | (ii)
-- src:2239 | after damages are assessed or accounts are taken by a District Judge; or
-- src:2240 | (iii)
-- src:2241 | in an application for a committal order for contempt of court;
-- src:2242 | ( b )
-- src:2243 | an appeal against any judgment of the General Division (except a judgment of the Registrar of the Supreme Court);
-- src:2244 | ( c )
-- src:2245 | an appeal against any judgment of the Appellate Division;
-- src:2246 | ( d )
-- src:2247 | an appeal from any tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal pursuant to any written law;
-- src:2248 | ( e )
-- src:2249 | an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal mentioned in paragraph ( a ), ( b ), ( c ) or ( d ); and
-- src:2250 | ( f )
-- src:2251 | an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act.
@ref O 19 r 1(a) to (f) (src:2235-2251)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` j THEN
        IF   (   j's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`
              OR j's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `District Court`)
         AND (   (    j's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`
                  AND j's `o 19 r 1 the proceedings began with` EQUALS `Originating claim`)
              OR (    j's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(a) a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent`
                  AND j's `o 19 r 1 the proceedings began with` EQUALS `Originating claim`)
              OR (    j's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`
                  AND j's `o 19 r 1 damages or accounts by a District Judge`)
              OR j's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (a) names three kinds of judgment of those courts; a judgment of another kind is not mentioned
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks only of "an appeal against any judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court"

@ref O 19 r 1(b) (src:2242-2243)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` j THEN
        BRANCH
            IF j's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `General Division` AND j's `o 19 r 1 who gave it` EQUALS `The Registrar`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except a judgment of the Registrar of the Supreme Court"
            IF j's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `General Division`
                THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks only of a judgment of the General Division
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks only of "an appeal against any judgment of the General Division"

@ref O 19 r 1(c) (src:2244-2245)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1(c) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` j THEN
        IF j's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) speaks only of a judgment of the Appellate Division
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) speaks only of "an appeal against any judgment of the Appellate Division"

@ref O 19 r 1(d) (src:2246-2247)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1(d) this Order applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` toAppellate pursuant THEN
        IF toAppellate AND pursuant
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (d) speaks only of an appeal "to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal pursuant to any written law"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (d) speaks only of "an appeal from any tribunal"

@ref O 19 r 1(e) (src:2248-2249)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1(e) this Order applies to an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 19 r 1 an application to the appellate Court` related THEN
        IF related
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (e) speaks only of an application "relating to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (e) speaks only of "an application to the appellate Court"

@ref O 19 r 1(f) (src:2250-2251)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1(f) this Order applies to an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (f) speaks only of "an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act"

-- Gathered by hand (option B of ruling E1, guidance for hand-gathering only; the six limbs above each answer on their own).
-- The one JUST FALSE is the Registrar exception inside limb (b); no other limb reaches a Registrar's judgment of the General Division.
@ref O 19 r 1 (src:2235-2251)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 1 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 1 this Order applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` matter EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` matter EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 1(c) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` matter EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 1(d) this Order applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` matter EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 1(e) this Order applies to an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal` matter EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 1(f) this Order applies to an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal` matter EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` matter EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except a judgment of the Registrar of the Supreme Court"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 1 lists six kinds of matter and does not say "only"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- general matters and structure of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Paragraph (1).  The Order yields to a written law on the right to appeal and on any requirement to apply for permission.
-- Which written law is outside these sources (the Supreme Court of Judicature Act is not among them), so it is an input.
-- src:2253 | 2. —(1) This Order is subject to any written law on the right to appeal and any requirement to apply for permission to appeal. (2) Division 2 of this Order concerns appeals from the District Court or the Magistrate’s Court to the General Division.
-- src:2254 | (3) Division 3 of this Order concerns — ( a )
-- src:2255 | appeals from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal (including appeals transferred between the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal);
-- src:2256 | ( b )
-- src:2257 | appeals from any tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal pursuant to any written law; and
-- src:2258 | ( c )
-- src:2259 | appeals from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal.
-- src:2260 | (4) Division 4 of this Order concerns appeals to the General Division against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act.
@ref O 19 r 2 (src:2253-2260)
GIVEN `a written law on the right to appeal or on a requirement to apply for permission to appeal applies to the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 2(1) this Order yields to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` MEANS
    IF `a written law on the right to appeal or on a requirement to apply for permission to appeal applies to the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1) says what this Order yields to; it does not say what follows when no such written law applies

-- Paragraphs (2) to (4).  Where an appeal comes from and goes to decides which Division "concerns" it.
DECLARE `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` HAS
    `o 19 r 2 appealed from` IS A `Court level`
    `o 19 r 2 appealed to` IS A `Court level`
    `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 2 from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `o 19 r 2 Division` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 2 Division 2`
    `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
    `o 19 r 2 Division 4`
    `o 19 r 2 no Division is named for the route`

@ref O 19 r 2(2) (src:2253)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 2(2) Division 2 concerns the appeal from the District Court or the Magistrate's Court to the General Division` MEANS
    IF       NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`)
        AND  NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`)
        AND (   route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `District Court`
             OR route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`)
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `General Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Division 2 of this Order concerns appeals from the District Court or the Magistrate’s Court to the General Division" does not say Division 2 concerns only those

@ref O 19 r 2(3)(a) (src:2254-2259)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 2(3)(a) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF       NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`)
        AND  NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`)
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `General Division`
        AND (   route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
             OR route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (3)(a) does not say Division 3 concerns only these appeals

@ref O 19 r 2(3)(b) (src:2256-2257)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 2(3)(b) Division 3 concerns the appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF       route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`
        AND (   route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
             OR route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (3)(b) does not say Division 3 concerns only these appeals

@ref O 19 r 2(3)(c) (src:2258-2259)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 2(3)(c) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF       NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`)
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (3)(c) does not say Division 3 concerns only these appeals

@ref O 19 r 2(4) (src:2260)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 2(4) Division 4 concerns the appeal to the General Division from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` MEANS
    IF       route's `o 19 r 2 from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `General Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (4) does not say Division 4 concerns only these appeals

-- Gathered by hand (option B of ruling E1, guidance only): which Division the text names for the route.
@ref O 19 r 2(2) to (4) (src:2253-2260)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A `o 19 r 2 Division`
`o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 19 r 2(2) Division 2 concerns the appeal from the District Court or the Magistrate's Court to the General Division` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `o 19 r 2 Division 2`
        IF `o 19 r 2(3)(a) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
        IF `o 19 r 2(3)(b) Division 3 concerns the appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
        IF `o 19 r 2(3)(c) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
        IF `o 19 r 2(4) Division 4 concerns the appeal to the General Division from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `o 19 r 2 Division 4`
        OTHERWISE `o 19 r 2 no Division is named for the route` -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (2) to (4) name three routes and say "concerns", not "only"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every defined term below opens "In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires".  The keel takes that as one input
-- (`o 1 r 3(1) a defined term has its defined meaning`) and a part does not thread it (PLAN.md section 7, item 9); the same holds here.

-- The documents the definitions name.
DECLARE `o 19 r 3 document` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 3 a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court`
    `o 19 r 3 the extracted order of the lower Court`
    `o 19 r 3 a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal`
    `o 19 r 3 an index cross-referencing each document to the record of appeal or supplemental record of appeal`
    `o 19 r 3 the order granting permission to appeal`
    `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal`
    `o 19 r 3 the certificate for security for costs`
    `o 19 r 3 the record of proceedings`
    `o 19 r 3 an affidavit of evidence-in-chief`
    `o 19 r 3 another document filed in the lower Court`
    `o 19 r 3 the certified transcript of the official record of hearing taken at the hearing of the cause or matter`
    `o 19 r 3 a compilation of authorities for the appeal`
    `o 19 r 3 any other document`

-- "bundle of authorities" means a compilation of authorities for the appeal, including case authorities, statutes and law journal articles.
DECLARE `o 19 r 3 authority` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 3 a case authority`
    `o 19 r 3 a statute`
    `o 19 r 3 a law journal article`
    `o 19 r 3 any other item`

-- src:2262 | 3. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires — “bundle of authorities” means a compilation of authorities for the appeal, including case authorities, statutes and law journal articles;
@ref O 19 r 3 "bundle of authorities" (src:2262)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 3 document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a document is a bundle of authorities` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `o 19 r 3 a compilation of authorities for the appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“bundle of authorities” means a compilation of authorities for the appeal"

@ref O 19 r 3 "bundle of authorities", including (src:2262)
GIVEN item IS A `o 19 r 3 authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 an item may be in a bundle of authorities` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS `o 19 r 3 any other item`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including case authorities, statutes and law journal articles" does not close the list
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2263 | “core bundle of documents” means a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court, the extracted order of the lower Court, a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal and an index cross‑referencing each document to the record of appeal or supplemental record of appeal;
@ref O 19 r 3 "core bundle of documents" (src:2263)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 3 document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the extracted order of the lower Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 an index cross-referencing each document to the record of appeal or supplemental record of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“core bundle of documents” means a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court, the extracted order of the lower Court, a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal and an index"

-- "judgment" means a judgment given by the lower Court in (a) to (e).
-- src:2264 | “judgment” means a judgment given by the lower Court — ( a )
-- src:2265 | in a trial, and includes a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent;
-- src:2266 | ( b )
-- src:2267 | after damages are assessed or accounts are taken;
-- src:2268 | ( c )
-- src:2269 | in an application for a committal order for contempt of court;
-- src:2270 | ( d )
-- src:2271 | in an application for a prerogative order; or
-- src:2272 | ( e )
-- src:2273 | in an appeal against a judgment described in paragraphs ( a ) to ( d );
@ref O 19 r 3 "judgment" (src:2264-2273)
GIVEN `it was given by the lower Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `o 19 r 3 kind of decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it was given by the lower Court`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“judgment” means a judgment given by the lower Court"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 19 r 3 any other decision`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“judgment” means a judgment given by the lower Court — (a) in a trial ... (e)", a closed list
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2274 | “record of appeal” means the order granting permission to appeal (if any), the notice of appeal, the certificate for security for costs, the record of proceedings, the affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief (if any), and all documents filed in the lower Court (so far as are relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal);
@ref O 19 r 3 "record of appeal" (src:2274)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 3 document`
      `it is relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the order granting permission to appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the certificate for security for costs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the record of proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 an affidavit of evidence-in-chief` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 another document filed in the lower Court` THEN
        IF `it is relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all documents filed in the lower Court (so far as are relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal)"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“record of appeal” means the order granting permission to appeal (if any), the notice of appeal, the certificate for security for costs, the record of proceedings, the affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief (if any), and all documents filed in the lower Court"

-- src:2275 | “record of proceedings” means a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision (if any) of the lower Court, the extracted order of the lower Court, and, in an appeal from the General Division, District Court or Magistrate’s Court, the certified transcript of the official record of hearing taken at the hearing of the cause or matter;
@ref O 19 r 3 "record of proceedings" (src:2275)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 3 document`
      `the appeal is from the General Division, the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the extracted order of the lower Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the certified transcript of the official record of hearing taken at the hearing of the cause or matter` THEN
        IF `the appeal is from the General Division, the District Court or the Magistrate's Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and, in an appeal from the General Division, District Court or Magistrate’s Court, the certified transcript" -- the transcript is named only for those appeals
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“record of proceedings” means a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision (if any) of the lower Court, the extracted order of the lower Court, and ... the certified transcript"

-- src:2276 | “second core bundle” means a compilation of the whole or part of the documents not included in the appellant’s or respondent’s core bundle of documents which are essential to the appeal and an index cross‑referencing each document to the record of appeal;
@ref O 19 r 3 "second core bundle" (src:2276)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 3 document`
      `it is already in the appellant's or respondent's core bundle of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a document is part of the second core bundle` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal` THEN
        IF `it is already in the appellant's or respondent's core bundle of documents`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not included in the appellant’s or respondent’s core bundle of documents"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 an index cross-referencing each document to the record of appeal or supplemental record of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“second core bundle” means a compilation of the whole or part of the documents ... and an index cross‑referencing each document to the record of appeal"

-- "trial" means the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application and includes all applications
-- taken out or heard on the same day as such hearing and at any time after its commencement until the giving of the judgment.
DECLARE `o 19 r 3 proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 3 the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application`
    `o 19 r 3 an application taken out or heard on the same day as such hearing`
    `o 19 r 3 an application taken out or heard after the commencement of such hearing and before the judgment is given`
    `o 19 r 3 any other proceeding`

-- src:2277 | “trial” means the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application and includes all applications taken out or heard on the same day as such hearing and at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment.
@ref O 19 r 3 "trial" (src:2277)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 19 r 3 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 3 a proceeding is part of the trial` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 an application taken out or heard on the same day as such hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 3 an application taken out or heard after the commencement of such hearing and before the judgment is given` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trial” means the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application and includes all applications taken out or heard on the same day"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- when time for appeal starts to run`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- This rule only says WHEN the time for an appeal or for an application for permission starts to run.
-- The period itself is in rule 14, 15, 25 or 26, and the count is O 3 r 3 (roc1).  "Starts to run from" a date (paragraph (2)(b))
-- and "starts to run after" a date (paragraphs (1), (1A)) both mean, by O 3 r 3(3), that the period begins immediately after that date;
-- every function here therefore answers with the date AFTER WHICH the time runs (fork F3 in NOTES.md).

-- What the lower Court has done about the issue of costs.
DECLARE `o 19 r 4(2)(a) what the lower Court has done about costs` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(i) decided on the parties' entitlement to costs, even if the amount of costs or disbursements has not been determined`
    `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(ii) ordered that costs be assessed`
    `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(iii) ordered that costs be reserved`
    `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(iv) decided that there is to be no order as to costs or that each party is to bear its own costs`
    `o 19 r 4(2)(a) none of these`

-- src:2279 | 4. —(1) Subject to any written law and paragraphs (1A) and (2), unless the Court otherwise orders, the time for the filing of an appeal or for the filing of an application for permission to appeal does not start to run until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the trial, including costs. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
-- src:2280 | (1A) Where the lower Court does not hear and determine the issue of costs within 30 days after the lower Court has heard and determined all other matters in the trial, the time for the filing of an appeal or for the filing of an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the expiry of the 30‑day period, even if the lower Court has directed that submissions on costs be made. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
-- src:2281 | (2) For the purposes of this Rule — ( a )
-- src:2282 | the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs when it has — (i)
-- src:2283 | decided on the parties’ entitlement to costs, even if the amount of costs or disbursements has not been determined;
-- src:2284 | (ii)
-- src:2285 | ordered that costs be assessed;
-- src:2286 | (iii)
-- src:2287 | ordered that costs be reserved; or
-- src:2288 | (iv)
-- src:2289 | decided that there is to be no order as to costs or that each party is to bear its own costs.; and
-- src:2290 | ( b )
-- src:2291 | in the case of a bifurcated trial, where the lower Court has heard and determined a distinct bifurcated portion of the trial (including the issue of costs), the time for the filing of an appeal or for the filing of an application for permission to appeal in respect of the bifurcated portion so determined starts to run from the date of that determination. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
@ref O 19 r 4 (src:2279-2291)
GIVEN done IS A `o 19 r 4(2)(a) what the lower Court has done about costs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 4(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` MEANS
    IF done EQUALS `o 19 r 4(2)(a) none of these`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs when it has" -- "when" counts as "where", and it has done none of (i) to (iv)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Paragraph (1): the time does not start until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the trial, including costs.
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all matters in the trial, including costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 19 r 4(1) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` MEANS
    `the date the lower Court heard and determined all matters in the trial, including costs` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): when the date is not yet known there is no start date to give

-- Paragraph (1A): costs not determined within 30 days after all other matters.
-- The 30 days are a period fixed in the text's own words.
`o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 30
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 19 r 4(1A) (src:2280)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        IF costs AT MOST `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` PLUS `o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs`'s `period length`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the lower Court does not hear and determine the issue of costs within 30 days" -- it did, so the paragraph does not apply
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` PLUS `o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs`'s `period length`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 30 days have not run out and costs are not yet determined, so the text does not yet say that the issue of costs was not determined within them

@ref O 19 r 4(1A) (src:2280)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 19 r 4(1A) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` MEANS
    IF `o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date asked about` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` PLUS `o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs`'s `period length`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph does not apply, or not yet: there is no date to give

-- Paragraph (2)(b): a bifurcated trial.  The result is a date, so the yes/no twin comes first.
@ref O 19 r 4(2)(b) (src:2290-2291)
GIVEN `the trial is bifurcated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lower Court has heard and determined a distinct bifurcated portion of the trial, including the issue of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 4(2)(b) this paragraph applies to a bifurcated portion` MEANS
    IF `the trial is bifurcated` AND `the lower Court has heard and determined a distinct bifurcated portion of the trial, including the issue of costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a bifurcated trial, where the lower Court has heard and determined a distinct bifurcated portion of the trial (including the issue of costs)" -- a "where" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 4(2)(b) (src:2290-2291)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined the distinct bifurcated portion, including the issue of costs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 19 r 4(2)(b) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run for the bifurcated portion` MEANS
    JUST `the date the lower Court heard and determined the distinct bifurcated portion, including the issue of costs`

-- Paragraph (1) read with (1A) and the exceptions, gathered by hand (option B of ruling E1, guidance only).
-- "Subject to any written law ... unless the Court otherwise orders": either is an input.
@ref O 19 r 4(1) and (1A) (src:2279-2280)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date asked about` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN `o 19 r 4(1A) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date asked about`
        IF `a written law provides otherwise` OR `the Court otherwise orders`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law", "unless the Court otherwise orders" -- what the law or the order says is not in these sources; paragraph (1A) is not made subject to either
        OTHERWISE `o 19 r 4(1) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`

-- The "until" bar, as its own yes/no function (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE before the start date, JUST FALSE after it.
@ref O 19 r 4(1) (src:2279)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court otherwise orders`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders" -- the bar does not hold when the Court has ordered otherwise
        IF `a written law provides otherwise`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date asked about` `a written law provides otherwise` `the Court otherwise orders`
            WHEN JUST start THEN
                IF `the date asked about` AT MOST start
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not start to run until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the trial, including costs" -- that has happened
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

-- Paragraphs (1) and (1A) read together.  (1A) is a positive start: once the 30 days have run out without costs being determined, time "starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period", so "has started" is JUST TRUE on the day after them whether costs are undecided or decided later.
-- Paragraph (1) is only the bar: before the start date "has started" is JUST FALSE.  The bar alone never makes it JUST TRUE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)), so every other day is NOTHING.
@ref O 19 r 4(1) and (1A) (src:2279-2280)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date asked about` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the date asked about` GREATER THAN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` PLUS `o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs`'s `period length`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date asked about` `a written law provides otherwise` `the Court otherwise orders` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not start to run until after" -- the bar holds
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar does not hold and (1A) does not start time, so the paragraphs do not say that it has started; a written law or an order may displace paragraph (1)

