§§ `Rule 5 -- permission to intervene`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2293 | 5. —(1) A person who is not a party in the appeal may apply to intervene in the appeal with the permission of the appellate Court. (2) The application for permission to intervene and the supporting affidavit must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal.
-- src:2294 | (3) The supporting affidavit must set out the applicant’s interest in the appeal.
-- src:2295 | (4) The appellate Court may impose conditions when the appellate Court grants permission to intervene, including ordering the intervening party to provide security for costs to any or all of the parties in the appeal.
@ref O 19 r 5 (src:2293-2295)
GIVEN `the person is a party in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 5(1) a person may apply to intervene in the appeal with the permission of the appellate Court` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party in the appeal`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks only of "A person who is not a party in the appeal"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 5(2) (src:2293)
GIVEN `the application for permission to intervene is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supporting affidavit is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both are served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 5(2) the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as required` MEANS
    IF `the application for permission to intervene is filed` AND `the supporting affidavit is filed` AND `both are served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application for permission to intervene and the supporting affidavit must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal"

@ref O 19 r 5(3) (src:2294)
GIVEN `the supporting affidavit sets out the applicant's interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 5(3) the supporting affidavit sets out the applicant's interest` MEANS
    IF `the supporting affidavit sets out the applicant's interest in the appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The supporting affidavit must set out the applicant’s interest in the appeal"

@ref O 19 r 5(4) (src:2295)
GIVEN `the appellate Court grants permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 5(4) the appellate Court may impose conditions on the permission to intervene` MEANS
    IF `the appellate Court grants permission to intervene`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appellate Court may impose conditions when the appellate Court grants permission to intervene" -- a "when" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 5(4) (src:2295)
GIVEN `the appellate Court grants permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition orders the intervening party to provide security for costs to any or all of the parties in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 5(4) the condition of security for costs may be imposed on an intervening party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appellate Court grants permission to intervene`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the appellate Court grants permission to intervene" -- a "when" that is not met
        IF `the condition orders the intervening party to provide security for costs to any or all of the parties in the appeal`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including ordering the intervening party to provide security for costs" names one condition and does not close the list

